    "q-73985": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73985",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨3,2,-3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩=6.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ ⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ 5(2+3t)-2(2t)+3(2-3t) & =6 \\\\ 10+15t-4t+6-9t & =6 \\\\ 2t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+3(-5),2(-5),2-3(-5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-10,17⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-13,-10,17).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
