    "q-108309": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108309",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,-1⟩+t⟨-1,2,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩=11.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ -2(2-t)+1(3+2t)+4(-1+3t) & =11 \\\\ -4+2t+3+2t-4+12t & =11 \\\\ 16t & =16 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-1,3+2(1),-1+3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,5,2).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
